1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,900
Every city has a history. But what happens
when its people can no longer remember it?

2
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:13,300
Here, even the past has a price.

3
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:24,700
Somewhere in this city, someone is borrowing
against its future. And the truth is buried
in the memories people have already surrendered.

4
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:33,600
Your memories can buy you time. But the lender
only sees what they can be sold for.

5
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:50,300
But a memory is more than collateral.
Your mother's voice can reveal a hidden truth.
Your childhood home can uncover something the
city has buried. The face you remember can open
doors that money alone cannot.

6
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:57,800
Some things are worth more while you still have them.

7
00:00:57,800 --> 00:01:05,500
And time is not on your side.
Every cycle adds to what you owe.

8
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:07,800
Still, the city has not forgotten everything.
Every clue brings you closer to the truth.

9
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:15,600
You can settle the debt. You can reclaim what
you pledged. But the choices you made have already
shaped the journey.

10
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:21,500
Because the question was never just what your
memories were worth.

11
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:25,000
It was what you were willing to lose to discover
the truth.

12
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:56,000
LACUNA. The price of remembering.